<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

  <!--
    Nop.Plugin.Feed.GoogleShopping - task 11.2
    (Requirements 5.5, 1.1-1.5, 2.4, 4.2, 5.1, 5.3, 3.1).

    THE RECIPE THIS FOLLOWS is the annotated
    src/Plugins/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles/Nop.Plugin.DiscountRules.CustomerRoles.csproj
    (task 10.1). Read that file for the reasoning behind the four silently-failing decisions and
    the fifth (Content Include vs Update for non-.cshtml content). Only what is DIFFERENT about
    this plugin is documented here.

    ===================================================================================
    WHAT IS DIFFERENT (1) - AN EmbeddedResource, AND IT IS NOT DECORATIVE
    ===================================================================================
    Files\taxonomy.txt is a 6000-line list of Google product categories, and
    Services/GoogleService.GetTaxonomyList() reads it with

        assem.GetManifestResourceStream("Nop.Plugin.Feed.GoogleShopping.Files.taxonomy.txt")

    i.e. by MANIFEST RESOURCE NAME, which the SDK derives from $(RootNamespace) plus the file's
    path with separators replaced by dots. RootNamespace defaults to $(AssemblyName), which is
    already Nop.Plugin.Feed.GoogleShopping, so the derived name is byte-identical to 3.90's and
    the call site needs no edit. It is restated in the ItemGroup below purely so this file
    declares it - the default Content/None globs would otherwise claim the file and it would ship
    as a loose deployed file whose stream lookup returns null, at which point the "Default Google
    category" dropdown on the configuration page is silently EMPTY and every feed generation
    throws NopException("Default Google category is not set"). Asserted by
    Nop.Web.SmokeTests.PluginViewRenderTests.

    ===================================================================================
    WHAT IS DIFFERENT (2) - STATIC ASSETS (runtime deferral 10.x-1)
    ===================================================================================
    Content\styles.css is referenced by ordinary URL from Views/Configure.cshtml as
    ~/Plugins/Feed.GoogleShopping/Content/styles.css, so it is deployed as a loose file
    (CopyToOutputDirectory="Always", as in 3.90) AND requires the NopStaticFileProvider allow-list
    entry task 11.1 added. See the equivalent block in
    Nop.Plugin.ExternalAuth.Facebook.csproj and the remarks on
    NopStaticFileProvider.AllowedPluginRoots.

    ===================================================================================
    WHAT IS DIFFERENT (3) - THIS PLUGIN HAS ITS OWN DbContext (runtime deferral 4.10)
    ===================================================================================
    Data\GoogleProductObjectContext.cs is an EF context of its own, registered by
    DependencyRegistrar through Nop.Web.Framework's RegisterPluginDataContext. It is therefore
    the first of the four plugin contexts deferral 4.10 names, and it is why this project
    references Nop.Data DIRECTLY - the legacy project did too, alongside EF6 <Reference>s that
    are NOT restated here: EntityFramework 6.1.3 and EntityFramework.SqlServer have no place in
    this solution any more, and EF Core arrives transitively through Nop.Data (task 3.1).

    ===================================================================================
    DROPPED IN THE CLASSIC -> SDK CONVERSION (Requirements 1.4, 1.5)
    ===================================================================================
    As in the 10.1 template: ToolsVersion/DefaultTargets/xmlns, ProjectGuid, ProductVersion,
    SchemaVersion, FileAlignment, AppDesignerFolder, OutputType, TargetFrameworkProfile,
    NuGetPackageImportStamp, TargetFrameworkVersion v4.5.1, Prefer32Bit, ErrorReport,
    WarningLevel, DefineConstants and the Debug/Release DebugType/DebugSymbols/Optimize blocks;
    the explicit <Compile Include> list of 12 files; the Microsoft.CSharp.targets import, the
    Microsoft.Bcl.Build.targets import and its EnsureNuGetPackageBuildImports guard, and the
    commented BeforeBuild/AfterBuild stubs.

    Every <Reference> with a HintPath into ..\..\packages\ is gone: the Microsoft.AspNet.Mvc
    5.2.3 / Razor 3.2.3 / WebPages 3.2.3 System.Web MVC stack, Autofac (transitive now),
    EntityFramework + EntityFramework.SqlServer (EF6, see above) and the net40/net45 polyfills
    Microsoft.Bcl.Async, Microsoft.Net.Http and Microsoft.Web.Infrastructure. The BCL
    <Reference>s are subsumed by the net10.0 shared framework, and
    <Reference Include="System.Web" /> has no net10.0 counterpart at all.

    app.config, packages.config and web.config are DELETED; web.config's load-bearing content is
    transcribed to Views/_ViewImports.cshtml. Properties/AssemblyInfo.cs is KEPT. Notes.txt stays
    non-deployed Content, as in 3.90.

    No <PackageReference>: this plugin has no third-party dependency of its own once EF6 is gone.
  -->

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <AddRazorSupportForMvc>true</AddRazorSupportForMvc>
    <StaticWebAssetsEnabled>false</StaticWebAssetsEnabled>
    <OutputPath>..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web\Plugins\Feed.GoogleShopping\</OutputPath>
    <AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>false</AppendTargetFrameworkToOutputPath>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Required explicitly - Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor does not add it implicitly. The controller binds
    Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc (+ .Rendering for SelectListItem), the plugin class binds
    Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing (RouteValueDictionary, on IMiscPlugin's GetConfigurationRoute)
    and the view binds Microsoft.AspNetCore.Routing as well.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Core\Nop.Core.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Data\Nop.Data.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Libraries\Nop.Services\Nop.Services.csproj" Private="false" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Presentation\Nop.Web.Framework\Nop.Web.Framework.csproj" Private="false" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Private="false" alone is NOT sufficient - see runtime-deferrals.md section 83.3. Note this
    plugin is the case that makes the point sharpest: it references Nop.Data DIRECTLY, so
    Nop.Data.dll would be copied here by name rather than by transitive accident, and
    PluginManager would shadow-copy and load it as the process's Nop.Data. Verbatim from the
    template; the "Nop." prefix filter keeps Payments.PayPalDirect's private PayPal SDK working
    (task 12.3).
  -->
  <Target Name="NopPluginDoNotDeployHostAssemblies" AfterTargets="ResolveReferences">
    <ItemGroup>
      <ReferenceCopyLocalPaths
          Remove="@(ReferenceCopyLocalPaths)"
          Condition="$([System.String]::Copy('%(Filename)').StartsWith('Nop.'))" />
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

  <!--
    View resolution. %(Link) becomes the compiled Razor identifier, so the view compiles as
    /Plugins/Feed.GoogleShopping/Views/Configure.cshtml and the controller's
    View("~/Plugins/Feed.GoogleShopping/Views/Configure.cshtml", model) call site stays UNEDITED.
    %(RecursiveDir) already contains "Views/" - do not repeat it.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Content Update="Views\**\*.cshtml"
             Link="Plugins\Feed.GoogleShopping\%(RecursiveDir)%(Filename)%(Extension)"
             CopyToOutputDirectory="Never" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    The manifest resource - see "WHAT IS DIFFERENT (1)". The <None Remove> keeps the file in
    exactly one item type so it is not ALSO deployed as loose content, which is what 3.90 did
    (its Content glob did not claim it).
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Remove="Files\taxonomy.txt" />
    <EmbeddedResource Include="Files\taxonomy.txt" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    Runtime-read content, deployed exactly as in 3.90. Include, NOT Update - AND the <None Remove>
    first; under Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor the default Content glob covers only .cshtml/.razor, so a
    bare <Content Update="Description.txt"> would match NOTHING and PluginManager could not see
    the plugin at all.

      Description.txt   parsed by PluginManager.Initialize. NOTE its SystemName is
                        "PromotionFeed.Froogle", NOT "Feed.GoogleShopping" - the plugin was
                        renamed upstream and the system name was not, and
                        FeedGoogleShoppingController.GenerateFeed looks the plugin up BY THAT
                        STRING. SupportedVersions must contain NopVersion.CurrentVersion
                        ("3.90"); both facts are asserted rather than assumed by
                        Nop.Web.SmokeTests.PluginViewRenderTests.
      logo.jpg          shown by the admin plugin list.
      Notes.txt         3.90 declared it Content with no CopyToOutputDirectory, i.e. not deployed.
      Content\**        the static asset tree - see "WHAT IS DIFFERENT (2)". A recursive glob
                        rather than 3.90's single explicit entry so an added asset cannot be
                        silently left undeployed; it currently matches exactly styles.css.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <None Remove="Description.txt" />
    <None Remove="logo.jpg" />
    <None Remove="Notes.txt" />
    <None Remove="Content\**" />
    <Content Include="Description.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="PreserveNewest" />
    <Content Include="logo.jpg" CopyToOutputDirectory="Always" />
    <Content Include="Notes.txt" CopyToOutputDirectory="Never" />
    <Content Include="Content\**" CopyToOutputDirectory="Always" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
